  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that switching the RNA encoder from PCA to SCVI in the best multimodal setup (ViT-L, avgpool, weighted) yielded the largest single improvement (0.635→0.706 acc, config_025→config_037). However, the SCGI encoder is completely untested across all experiments. Config_049 (scgpt + ViT-L + avgpool + weighted) is the direct counterpart to config_037, isolating the RNA encoder choice while holding all other design decisions at their best-performing values. This experiment will clarify whether SCGI offers a comparable or superior representation to SCVI in the multimodal setting. If SCGI matches or exceeds SCVI, it opens a new optimization direction; if it underperforms, it confirms SCVI as the preferred encoder and allows us to focus remaining budget on aggregation/fusion refinements around SCVI. Under a limited budget, testing the single largest unexplored variable in the top-performing configuration is the highest-information next step."
}

